# Coelho: your own schema

```elixir
Mix.install([
  # Coelho.Kino is on Hex from 0.18; until then, from GitHub.
  {:coelho, github: "nseaSeb/coelho"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.19"},
  {:phoenix_live_view, "~> 1.1"}
])
```

## One schema, both halves

A schema is declared once, in Elixir. The server validates and renders with it;
the browser builds its editor from the same declaration, exported as JSON. Add
a node of your own — a callout — to the shipped schema:

```elixir
schema =
  Coelho.Schema.extend(Coelho.Schema.default(),
    nodes: [
      callout: [
        group: "block",
        content: "inline*",
        attrs: [tone: [default: "info", validate: {:one_of, ~w(info warning)}]],
        render: {"aside", [{"class", "callout"}]}
      ]
    ]
  )

Map.keys(schema.nodes)
```

## The validator is the schema

The schema says what a document may hold, and nothing else gets through:

```elixir
callout = fn tone ->
  %{
    "type" => "doc",
    "content" => [
      %{
        "type" => "callout",
        "attrs" => %{"tone" => tone},
        "content" => [%{"type" => "text", "text" => "Mind the gap"}]
      }
    ]
  }
end

%{
  info: Coelho.validate(callout.("info"), schema),
  panic: Coelho.validate(callout.("panic"), schema),
  without_the_node: Coelho.validate(callout.("info"), Coelho.Schema.default())
}
```

```elixir
{:ok, document} = Coelho.validate(callout.("warning"), schema)
Coelho.to_html(document, schema)
```

## An editor for it

The editor knows the node because the schema says so: no JavaScript to write.

```elixir
Coelho.Kino.new(schema: schema, value: document)
```

## Less, for one field

`restrict/2` narrows a schema to what one field may hold — a comment that takes
paragraphs, bold and italic, and nothing else. The toolbar follows.

```elixir
comment =
  Coelho.Schema.restrict(Coelho.Schema.default(),
    nodes: [:doc, :paragraph, :text],
    marks: [:bold, :italic]
  )

Coelho.Kino.new(schema: comment, placeholder: "A comment: bold and italic only")
```
